-- title:
--   (3.12) gives time-consistency (2.12)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $X$ is the recombining binomial tree of (3.11): nodes $x_{i,0}<\dots<x_{i,i}$ at time $t_i$ ($0\le i\le N$), up-probabilities $0<p^+_{i,j}<1$; $\varphi_{t_1},\dots,\varphi_{t_N}$ are distortion functions and $\varphi_{t_0}(p)=p$; $G_{i,j}=\mathbb P(X_{t_i}\ge x_{i,j})$, $G_{i,i+1}=0$; $q^\pm_{i,j}$ and $\mathbb Q$ are given by (3.13) and (3.15); and condition (3.14) holds.
--
--   Let $\Phi$ be a dynamic distortion function whose conditional nonlinear expectations satisfy (3.12) for every pair of times:
--   $$
--   \mathcal E_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]=\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}\bigl[g(X_{t_n})\mid\sigma(X_{t_i})\bigr],\qquad 0\le i<n\le N,\ g\in\mathcal I .
--   $$
--   Then $\Phi$ is time-consistent:
--   $$
--   \mathcal E_{t_i,t_m}\bigl[\mathcal E_{t_m,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]\bigr]=\mathcal E_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})],\qquad 0\le i<m<n\le N,\ g\in\mathcal I .
--   $$
--
--   The tower property of $\mathcal E$ is inherited from the tower property of the linear conditional expectation under $\mathbb Q$; the point is that $\mathcal E_{t_m,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]$ is again of the form $\tilde g(X_{t_m})$ with $\tilde g\in\mathcal I$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a Markov process X on an abstract filtered probability space with transition law (3.11) and the filtration F = F^X it generates → the canonical path space Fin N → Bool (true = up) with path weights ∏ p^±, and X_{t_i}(ω) = x_{i, number of up-moves before i}; reason: every quantity in the statement depends only on the law of X and on F^X; the same instances
--   - encoding: times 0 = t_0 < ⋯ < t_N → time indices 0, …, N (Φ(t_i, t_n, x; p) is Φ i n x p, φ_{t_n} is φ n); reason: the times enter only as labels
--   - encoding: the assumption φ_0(p) := p → phiExt φ 0 = id built into the definitions; the value φ 0 of the given family is ignored; reason: the same convention, without a hypothesis on φ 0
--   - encoding: conditioning on F_{t_i} (resp. σ(X_{t_i})) and identities between random variables → conditioning on the atom of F_{t_i} containing ω (resp. on the event {X_{t_i} = X_{t_i}(ω)}), identities stated at every path ω; reason: F_{t_i} = σ(X_{t_0}, …, X_{t_i}) is generated by these atoms, and every path has positive probability, so almost-sure identities are identities at every path
--   - encoding: ∫₀^∞ Φ(s, t, X_s; ℙ(ξ ≥ x | F_s)) dx → Bochner integral over (0, ∞) of the same integrand; reason: the integrand is bounded with bounded support for every ξ the statement uses, so the integral is finite and equals the paper's
--   - generalization: the dynamic distortion function Φ constructed in the proof → any dynamic distortion function Φ satisfying (3.12) for all 0 ≤ i < n ≤ N; reason: the page's argument uses only (3.12) and Lemma 3.3; the constructed Φ is an instance
-- source:
--   Ma–Wong–Zhang, Time-consistent conditional expectation under probability distortion, arXiv:1809.08262v5, https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.08262v5, proof of Theorem 3.4, display "𝓔_{t_i,t_m}[𝓔_{t_m,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]] = …", p.14

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Distortion
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Tree
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Dynamic

open MeasureTheory Set

namespace DistortedCondExp

/-- **(3.12) gives time-consistency** (Ma–Wong–Zhang, arXiv:1809.08262v5, proof of Theorem 3.4,
p.14: "fix `n` and `g` and let `u_i` be as in Lemma 3.3. Since `u_m` is increasing, we have
`𝓔_{t_i,t_m}[𝓔_{t_m,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]] = 𝓔_{t_i,t_m}[u_m(X_{t_m})] = u_i(X_{t_i}) = 𝓔_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]`,
`0 ≤ i < m < n`. This verifies (2.12)."). Under (3.14), a dynamic distortion function `Φ` that
satisfies (3.12), `𝓔_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})] = 𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_n}) | σ(X_{t_i})]` for all `0 ≤ i < n ≤ N`
and all `g ∈ ℐ`, is time-consistent (2.12).

**Formalization Note** `Satisfies312` is (3.12) for every pair of times, at every path;
`IsTimeConsistent` is (2.12) for `0 ≤ r < s < t ≤ N`, every `g ∈ ℐ` and every path. -/
theorem tower_of_eq_3_12 (N : ℕ) (x p : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (φ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ)
    (htree : IsBinomialTree N x p) (hφ : ∀ n, 1 ≤ n → n ≤ N → IsDistortion (φ n))
    (h314 : Cond314 N x p φ)
    (Φ : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (hΦ : IsDynamicDistortion N Φ) (h312 : Satisfies312 N x p φ Φ) :
    IsTimeConsistent N x p Φ := by sorry

end DistortedCondExp
